@DLord 27. "Blood," or "wine" = the good of faith from the Word.

@DLW 420. The chyle collected from things esculent and vinous.

@DP 254[4]. (The bränvin -vinum adjustum-* of a peasant, as opposed to the noble wine of a king.)
Footnote: * Vinum adustum is evidently a literal translation into Latin of the Swedish word "bränvin," which means a spirituous liquor that is made from potatoes.

@284[2]. Good (then) becomes like generous wine after fermentation... But if evil conquers, good with its truth... becomes turbid and foul, like unfermented wine...

@292[2]. The heat (that) flows into things vinous, fragrant, etc.

@AR 316. "Hurt not the oil and the wine" (Revelation 6:6) = that... the holy goods and truths which lie hidden in the Word be not violated and profaned. @AE 375.

@--. "Oil" = the good of love; "wine," truth from this good. Illustrated. @AE 375.

@--[3]. "They do not put new wine -venum novum- into old bottles..." (Matthew 9:17). "New wine" = the Divine truth of the New Testament, thus of the new Church; and "the old wine" = the Divine truth of the Old Testament, thus of the old Church. @AE 195[15].

@--[5]. That "wine" = holy truth, is evident from its opposite sense, in which it = truth falsified and profaned. Illustrated.

@417[9]. He said, I have planted a vineyard; I will now drink wine even to drunkenness... out of an invisible cup... But I say unto you, Drink wine from the Word understood. Explained.

@632. "She made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her fornication" (Revelation 14:8) = that by profanations of the Word, and adulterations of the good and truth of the Church, she has seduced all... "Wine" = truth from good; and, in the opposite sense, falsity from evil. @AE 881. See @AR 721. @758.

@635. "The wine of the anger of God mingled with unmixed" (Revelation 14:10) = the truth of the Word falsified, ( = falsity and the derivative evil, conjoined with falsified truths. @AE 887.)

@649[end]. Under <Vineyard>, see this reference.

@721. "Wine" = the Divine truth of the Word.

@758. "The wine" (Revelation 18:3) = their nefarious dogmas.

@778. "Wine" (Revelation 18:13) = truth from the good of love.

@795[end]. (They say) that the wine is for (the priests) lest they should be wearied out; and that water is mixed with the wine, lest they be inebriated.

@829. "The wine of the fury and anger of God" (Revelation 19:15) = the goods and truths of the Church, which are from the Word, profaned and adulterated; thus the evils and falsities of the Church.

@CL 3[3]. (Heavenly happiness supposed to consist in feasting, with) generous and noble wines.

@13[2]. The trees of wine (in the garden) came next to the trees of oil.

@14[2]. They saw a table magnificently laid out, containing... wine jellies -musta vinorum concreta-... and a pyramid through the middle of which there gushed out a fountain of nectareous wine...

@20[end]. (Wine drunk at a wedding in Heaven.)

@TCR 328. Compared to the taste of the wine that is pressed out of the grapes.

@377[end]. Like grapes after the wine has been pressed out of them.

@383[end]. Like urine conjoined with wine of flavour.

@702. That by the Lord's "blood," and by "the wine," is meant the Divine truth of His wisdom, and also all the truth of faith. General article.

@708. That by "wine" is meant the like as by "blood." Illustrated.

@834[end]. Like the fragrance in wine cellars -cellis vinariis-.

@WE 6400. The reason (the priests) did not drink wine or strong drink (Leviticus 10:9) was indeed from drunkenness... lest... the representations should be disturbed; for wine disturbs the life of the body and the natural life of the mind... so that the spiritual life cannot act in it becomingly...

@WE 6400. The flame in the Habitation, the shining gold, and the aromatic odour of the incense would have been disturbed by wine, and therefore the representations would have been disturbed; besides that the odour of the wine and strong drink would have united itself with the mind... so that it could not make a distinction between what was holy and what was profane. @WE 5523, Further explained.

@WE 6848. Thus the Nazarite might (then) drink wine... because it was after he had been sanctified; for then wine could not inebriate him. It is as it is with the regenerate, to whom cupidities then do no harm, because then the cupidities are no longer excited by nature and the body... The wine is thus happiness, or heavenly joy; for it then exhilarates, and excites only the things that are of charity. @6880.

@SE 2458. A disgust for wine, or intoxicating drink. See <Drunk>.

@3486. (Poisoned wine offered me by Dippel, the effect of which would have been to destroy the understanding.)

@3801[end]. (The Quaker Spirit) appeared with a flask of red or dark wine, which he drank up, and so disappeared. @3802. @3803, Explained. See @LJPost 59.

@3898. (Great goblets full of wine with sugar seen, with which the lascivious girls delighted themselves.)

@4053. Wine cellars seen, as representatives.

@6059. Why the Papists have separated the bread from the wine... It is not done on account of deficiency of wine, because there is wine in Italy, France, Spain, Portugal, the more interior part of Germany, and Hungary; and where wine is not produced, as in England, Holland, Sweden, Denmark, and Protestant Germany, wine does not grow - and yet it is employed in the sacrament of the Supper. The Papists could find no other reason except that the monks... should not be wearied out in their continuous labour... But it was said that it has come to pass of the Divine Providence... because good is not good if separated from truth... @AE 1054[end], Explained.

@AE 223[6]. "A cry over the wine in the streets" (Isaiah 24:11) = the truth of doctrine falsified, over which there is contest and indignation. (Compare @652[7].)

@235[7]. "They err through wine, through strong drink they go astray... they are swallowed up by wine" (Isaiah 28:7) = truths mixed with falsities.

@252[6]. "Wine" = the good of charity, which in its essence is truth. References.

@--[7]. "A feast of lees," that is, of the best wines (Isaiah 25:6) = the appropriation of truths.

@283[16]. "The wine is gone" (Hosea 4:17) = that the truth of the Church has departed. @376[38]. @887[4].

@329. In the Word... "wine" stands for all spiritual drink, (that is) all the truth which is communicated to man by the Lord.

@--[2]. Thus "wine" = the Divine truth proceeding from the Divine good of the Divine love; and, in relation to man, this received by him.

@--[4]. As by "wine" is meant the Divine truth nourishing the spiritual life, the Lord says... "I will not drink of this product of the vine... until I shall drink it new with you." ( = the good of faith which in its essence is truth. @376[26].)

@359[3]. In the winepresses, the wine is pressed out of the grapes; and "wine" = the Divine truth.

@376. That "wine" = spiritual good, which is the good of charity towards the neighbour and the good of faith; and... in its essence this good is truth... Hence it is that "wine" = truth. General article. @--[4], Illustrated.

@--[6]. "Must," that is, "wine" (Amos 9) = truth.

@--[13]. The derivative truths are meant by the "treading out of the wine in the winepresses" (Isaiah 16:10)... For they were wont to sing... in the winepresses when the grape was trodden into wine, on account of the representation of the delights from the truths which are signified by "wine."

@--[14]. The truths of good that were taken away, are meant by "the vintage," and "the wine in the winepresses" (Jeremiah 48:33).

@--[15]. "Corn and wine" (Lamentations 2:12) = all the good and truth of the Church in general. @750[13].

@--[19]. "The wine of Heshbon" (Ezekiel 27:18) = natural truth.

@--[22]. "Wine" (Zechariah 10:7) = the truth from good from which is this heavenly delight. @448[8].

@--[23]. To "drink wine out of the vessels of the Temple" (Daniel 5) = to imbibe the truths of the Church that are from the Word.

@--[24]. "Wine" (Joel 3:3) = truth falsified.

@--[25]. As "wine" = the truth of the Church which is from good... the libation of wine was commanded. Illustrated.

@--[26]. "The product of the vine," that is, wine, which the Lord would drink new with them... = that all the Divine truth in Heaven and the Church would then be from His Divine Human. He therefore calls it "new"; and He also calls it "the New Testament in My blood"; for the Lord's "blood" = the like as "wine."

@--[27]. The "wine" (as brought forth by Melchizedek, Genesis 14:18) = the Divine truth, or, in application to man... the good of faith which comes from the reception of the Divine truth.

@--[28]. In Luke 5:37-39, "wine" = truth; "old wine," the truth of the old or Jewish Church... And that the statutes and judgments of the Jewish Church... do not accord with the truths of the Christian Church, is meant by, "They do not put new wine into old bottles"... And that those who have been born and brought up in the external things of the Jewish Church cannot be at once brought into the internal things of the Christian Church, is signified by, "No one who drinks old wine straightway desires new; for he says, The old is more useful."

@--[29]. The like is signified by the water turned into wine... (which = ) the truth of the external Church, such as was that of the Jewish Church from the sense of the letter (made into) the truth of the internal Church, such as is that of the Christian Church... by opening the internal things concealed in the former.

@--[31]. "Wine," in the opposite, = truth falsified, and also falsity. Illustrated. @--[37].

@--. "Smitten down -perturbati- with wine" (Isaiah 28:1) = those who see falsity in place of truth... "These err through wine..." (Isaiah 28:7) = through falsities.

@--[32]. See <Strong drink>. @--[33].

@--[34]. "Every bottle shall be filled with wine" (Jeremiah 13:12) = the mind of man with falsity.

@--[37]. To be "inflamed with wine" (Isaiah 5:11) = to hatch doctrinal things from themselves.

@--. "Heroes to drink wine" (Isaiah 5:22) = those who aspire to great things (and who) imbibe falsities. ( = those who adulterate the truth of the Word. @618[3].)

@--[39]. "The wine of the wrath of God" = the falsity of evil.

@386. Natural foods correspond to spiritual foods; as... wine to truths from good.

@433[4]. "He washes his garment in wine" (Genesis 49:11) = the Lord's external or natural Human, that it is Divine truth from His Divine love; "and his vesture in the blood of grapes" = the Lord's internal or rational Human, that it is Divine good from His Divine love; "his eyes are redder than wine" = that the internal or rational Human is nothing but good...

@--[30]. "Their wine is the poison of dragons, and the cruel gall of asps" (Deuteronomy 32:33) = falsities from evil... "Wine" = truth from the Word; but "poison of dragons," and "gall of asps" = the monstrous falsity that comes forth from the falsified truths of the Word. (Compare @519[7]. @714[27].)

@444[14]. "Wine," in the Word, = the good and truth of faith. @519[7].

@448[8]. "Their heart shall be glad as if with wine" (Zechariah 10:7) = the joy of such from truths.

