@556[21]. "His eyes red with wine" = that His Intellectual was Divine truth from Divine good.

@617[26]. To "eat flesh and drink wine" (Isaiah 22:13) = to appropriate to one's self evil and falsity... "Wine" = the falsity of evil.

@638[6]. "The vine" = (the Spiritual Church) because... "wine" = the good of charity towards the neighbour and the good of faith.

@--[19]. To "plant a vineyard and cultivate it, and not to drink the wine" (Deuteronomy 28:39) = that although the Church is established, and the truths of doctrine are taught, still truths will not affect and perfect. "Wine" = the truth of doctrine.

@652[7]. "Wine" = the truth of the Church from the Word.

@727[2]. "My cup shall run over" = with the truth of doctrine from the Word; for "cup" here stands for "wine."

@863[10]. To "sell a girl for wine" (Joel 3:3) = to falsify the goods of the Word.

@918[9]. As all truth is from good, as all wine is from grapes, by "wine," in the Word, is signified truth from good. @922[6].

@919[4]. "Wine" = the truth of the Church.

